--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 [v1.0.0] — INITIAL BUILD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## 0. SOURCE AUDIT (performed before any code was written)

Scraped https://alohabroadband.com/ and its subpages to establish ground truth.

  Pages read:
    /                    homepage, feature grid, uptime and repair claims
    /pricing             plan names, prices, per-plan feature ticks, fee table
    /learn-more          how the point-to-point link works, security
    /fixed-wireless      latency figures, tower ownership, signal range
    /coverage            serviceable communities
    /support             FAQ source material, tier notes
    /testimonials        tone and regional references
    /contact-us          published business hours

  BRAND COLOURS — extracted from the live theme stylesheet
  (https://alohabroadband.com/wp-content/themes/Aloha/style.css).
  These are the carrier's actual hex values, not approximations:

    #012145  deep brand navy        #0066cc  action blue
    #091c30  deepest navy/charcoal  #bfd9f0  light blue
    #123e7a  mid blue               #dceefd  pale blue
    #5187c2  medium blue            #f2f7fc  near-white blue tint
    #8797a7  slate                  #c2d8eb  pale blue
    #8fa5b7  slate light            #d9e8f7  pale blue
    #ec6c27  brand orange           #313131  body ink
    #ff4b33  brand coral (used 10x in theme -> adopted as primary CTA)

  Derived tints/shades are labelled DERIVED in tailwind.config.ts and
  app/globals.css. No hue was invented.

  SERVICE LINE AUDIT — this is the most consequential finding.
  Aloha Broadband sells exactly ONE service line: fixed terrestrial wireless
  internet. Confirmed by HTTP probe (all 404) and by their own copy:

    /fiber    -> 404      /tv      -> 404      /bundles  -> 404
    /cable    -> 404      /mobile  -> 404      /business -> 404
    /phone    -> 404      /voip    -> 404

  Their /fixed-wireless page states the network uses "Fixed Terrestrial
  Wireless radio systems", explicitly not satellite and not fiber.

  Consequence under the "NO Missing Services" rule: the Fiber, Cable, Bundles,
  TV, Mobile and Phone sections are omitted entirely. They are not stubbed,
  not left empty, and carry no "call to ask" placeholder. The ServiceLine
  union still contains all six names, so if the carrier adds a line later,
  adding plans with that serviceLine makes the section appear automatically.

  "Voice over IP" appears on the carrier's plan table as a capability the
  connection supports, NOT as a phone product they sell. It is therefore
  listed as a plan feature and did not justify a Phone section.

  SPEEDS: the carrier publishes no Mbps figures for residential plans and
  states plans are "Best Effort, shared bandwidth... not guaranteed". No speed
  numbers were invented. PlanItem.speedDown / speedUp are left undefined and
  the UI falls back to PlanItem.capability, which carries the carrier's own
  stream-count tiering language. The card renders Mbps automatically the day
  those fields are populated.


## 1. PROJECT SCAFFOLD

  + package.json           Next.js 16.3.5, React 19.3.0, TypeScript 5.6,
                           Tailwind 3.4.19, Lenis 1.3.26.
                           npm audit: 0 vulnerabilities.
                           (Started on Next 14.2.15, which npm flagged for a
                           published security advisory; moved to 14.2.35, then
                           to 16 because 14's bundled PostCSS still carried a
                           critical advisory. Nothing was written yet, so the
                           major upgrade cost nothing.)
  + tsconfig.json          strict: true, @/* path alias.
  + next.config.mjs        reactStrictMode, poweredByHeader off, compress on.
  + postcss.config.mjs
  + tailwind.config.ts     Full Aloha palette, price-lockup type scale,
                           brand gradients, keyframes, silk/swoop easings.
  + .gitignore
  + .claude/launch.json    Dev server config (autoPort enabled).

  ! No backend, no API routes, no database. Strict frontend build.


## 2. DATA ARCHITECTURE (core requirement)

  + lib/content.ts         SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
                           Exports: ServiceLine, PlanItem, site, promos,
                           plans, serviceSections, finePrint,
                           finePrintDisclaimers, features, marqueeItems,
                           coverage, coverageBlurb, faqs, legalPages.
                           Derived helpers: plansForLine(),
                           activeServiceSections(), ctaLabelFor(),
                           lookupZip(), serviceableZips.

                           Every price, fee, feature, FAQ, coverage ZIP and
                           nav label on the site reads from this file. No
                           component hardcodes plan knowledge. Changing a
                           price means editing one line here.

                           PlanItem matches the specified interface exactly.
                           The ServiceLine union adds 'wireless' alongside the
                           six specified names, because that is the line the
                           carrier actually sells. Nothing was removed.

  + lib/legal.ts           Body copy for the eight legal documents.
  + lib/hooks.ts           useInView, usePrefersReducedMotion,
                           useActiveSection, useScrolled.


## 3. COMPONENTS

  UI primitives
  + components/ui/PriceLockup.tsx      REQUIRED universal component. The only
                                       place money is formatted: superscript
                                       $, oversized integer (2.5/3/3.5rem via
                                       the text-price-* scale), muted cents,
                                       muted cadence, sr-only full string.
                                       Falls back to a quote line when a plan
                                       has no published price.
  + components/ui/MagneticButton.tsx   Magnetic pointer-follow CTA, label
                                       trails at 0.4x for parallax. Skipped on
                                       touch and under reduced motion.
  + components/ui/TiltCard.tsx         3D tilt on mouse-move, reserved for the
                                       plan cards. Drives a --mx/--my specular
                                       highlight.
  + components/ui/primitives.tsx       Reveal, RevealHeading (per-word mask and
                                       rise), Wipe (clip-path section
                                       transition), Stagger (grid entrance),
                                       Parallax (rAF, transform-only),
                                       Marquee (infinite ticker).
  + components/ui/BlackHoleField.tsx   Hero deep-space canvas.
  + components/ui/SignalTrace.tsx      SVG path-draw schematic of the
                                       point-to-point tower topology.
  + components/ui/ZipChecker.tsx       Frontend-only ZIP lookup against the
                                       static coverage table. No network call.
  + components/ui/Icons.tsx            Inline SVG icon set.
  + components/SmoothScroll.tsx        Lenis, plus anchor routing through Lenis
                                       with sticky-header offset.

  Sections
  + components/sections/Header.tsx           Disclosure bar + sticky header.
  + components/sections/Hero.tsx             Hero.
  + components/sections/PlanCard.tsx         Plan card.
  + components/sections/ServiceSections.tsx  Service-line renderer.
  + components/sections/FinePrintGrid.tsx    Fine-print grid.
  + components/sections/WhyAloha.tsx         Feature grid + CTA band.
  + components/sections/Faq.tsx              Accordion.
  + components/sections/Footer.tsx           Legal footer.


## 4. PAGES

  + app/layout.tsx         Sora (display) + Inter (body) via next/font,
                           metadata, Open Graph, skip link, Lenis mount.
  + app/globals.css        Brand tokens, reveal/wipe/draw/tilt primitives,
                           full prefers-reduced-motion suppression.
  + app/page.tsx           Landing page in the strict required order, plus
                           FAQPage + Service JSON-LD.
  + app/[slug]/page.tsx    The eight legal pages. dynamicParams = false, so
                           only those eight slugs build and anything else
                           404s. All eight prerender as static HTML.


## 5. SECTION ORDER AS SHIPPED

   1. Top disclosure bar    "Independent Authorized Retailer of Aloha
                            Broadband." — persistent, above the header.
   2. Sticky header         Aloha-styled, anchor nav with scroll-spy
                            underline, "Call (808) 555-0142" CTA.
   3. Hero                  Live promos, H1, ZIP checker AND "Call to order"
                            button side by side, black-hole background,
                            trust ticker.
   4. Service lines         Fiber/Cable/Bundles/TV/Mobile/Phone all omitted
                            (carrier sells none). Fixed wireless renders,
                            closing with the coverage band (#coverage) and
                            the SVG signal trace.
   5. Fine-print grid       Included / one-time / optional, plus disclaimers.
   6. Why Aloha             Staggered feature grid, CTA band, reverse ticker.
   7. FAQ                   Ten-item accordion, sticky left rail.
   8. Footer                Reseller disclosure + the eight legal pages.


## 6. ANIMATION INVENTORY

  Implemented, all of them:
    Lenis smooth scrolling (mandatory)         SmoothScroll.tsx
    Black hole / deep-space hero background    BlackHoleField.tsx
    Scroll-triggered text reveals              RevealHeading, Reveal
    Parallax depth on background imagery       Parallax (hero, Why Aloha)
    SVG path draw                              SignalTrace + .draw-path
    Magnetic button hover on all CTAs          MagneticButton
    Clip-path wipe between major sections      Wipe + .wipe
    3D card tilt on the plan cards             TiltCard
    Staggered grid entrance                    Stagger (Why Aloha)
    Infinite marquee / ticker                  Marquee (hero + Why Aloha)

  Explicitly NOT used, per the bans:
    - No generic 3D spiral hero animation. The hero particles drift on
      straight vectors bent by a central mass; there is no vortex or helix.
    - No scroll-scrubbed animated assembly diagram anywhere. The SVG trace
      draws once on entry via a CSS transition; it is not tied to scroll
      position.

  Performance posture: zero animation libraries. Lenis is the only runtime
  dependency beyond React/Next. Everything else is CSS transitions driven by
  one shared IntersectionObserver contract. The canvas caps DPR at 2, runs
  ~150 particles, and its rAF loop is suspended whenever the hero leaves the
  viewport or the tab is hidden. Every effect is fully suppressed under
  prefers-reduced-motion.


## 7. NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS — VERIFIED AGAINST THE RENDERED DOM

   [PASS] No support routing. No instruction to contact the carrier for
          billing, outages or support. The carrier's published numbers
          ((808) 929-7668 / (800) 929-5583) appear nowhere in the codebase.
   [PASS] Hero contains BOTH the ZIP checker and a prominent Call button.
   [PASS] CTA text. Basic -> "Call to order". Standard -> "Call to order".
          Plus (no price) -> "Call for pricing". Derived by ctaLabelFor(),
          never hardcoded. Zero raw phone numbers as button text outside the
          header and footer (programmatically asserted).
   [PASS] No competitor bashing. Neither banned phrase appears. The carrier's
          own comparison copy about DSL/LTE/satellite was deliberately NOT
          reproduced; only neutral, factual statements about the technology
          were kept.
   [PASS] No missing-service placeholders. Six service lines omitted
          entirely.
   [PASS] No Broadband Facts label links.
   [PASS] No "Pricing observed [date]" stamps anywhere.
   [PASS] No fake FAQs. No "is this the official site" item and no FAQ
          explaining authorized-retailer legal structure. All ten questions
          are practical pre-sale questions.
   [PASS] Footer carries the reseller disclosure and exactly eight legal
          pages, all eight prerendered and reachable.


## 8. BUG FIXED DURING BUILD

  ! body { overflow-x: hidden } turned <body> into a scroll container, which
    silently broke position:sticky on the header — the header detached and
    drifted mid-page. Changed to overflow-x: clip, which suppresses horizontal
    scroll without establishing a scroll container. Verified: the header's
    bounding rect now resolves to top: 0 at every scroll offset.


## 9. ACTION REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH

  1. PHONE NUMBER. lib/content.ts -> site.phone is (808) 555-0142, a NANPA
     reserved fictional number used as a safe placeholder. Replace it with the
     retailer's own tracked sales line. It is referenced in exactly one place,
     so one edit updates the header, hero, every plan CTA and the footer.
  2. LEGAL REVIEW. lib/legal.ts contains complete, professionally drafted
     starting documents, but they are not legal advice. Have counsel review
     them against actual data flows, retention schedule and the retailer
     agreement, and fill in the entity name, postal address and privacy
     contact.
  3. metadataBase in app/layout.tsx is https://example.com. Point it at the
     production domain so Open Graph URLs resolve.
  4. Re-verify carrier pricing before go-live and on a recurring schedule.
     Everything lives in lib/content.ts.

